# SQ{n}

## Question
{One question the review answers.}

## Why it matters to the observation (step 0)
{One or two sentences.}

## Origin
{step 0 | notes | counter-evidence (added by skeptic)}

## Kind
{census | kinds | evidence}, because {why this question needs every instance, every kind of instance, or what the evidence says}. (`research/sls/1-protocol/step.md`, *How much each question needs*)

## Unit
{What counts as new for this question: an instance (e.g. "a system"), a kind (e.g. "a kind of message-based system"), or a finding (a claim, cause, measurement or counter-argument).}

## Enough when
{census: every distinct unit is covered by one read paper, and a search round finds no new one | kinds or evidence: at least {10} papers serving it are read, in the reading order, then {3} in a row add nothing new.}

## Reading order
{How the papers serving it are ordered, so saturation is not reached on similar papers: e.g. both sides alternating, different groups and decades, strongest first.}

{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "decision-card.schema.json",
  "title": "Decision card",
  "description": "One decision that is mine, as an agent proposes it and a gate asks it (ai/gate.md, *Decision card*). The plain part is what I read; the edits are what the option does. Agents return each decision as a ```json block with this shape.",
  "type": "object",
  "required": ["target", "situation", "why_it_matters", "question", "options"],
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
    "target": {
      "description": "The file the decision is about, relative to research/.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "situation": {
      "description": "What is being decided and why it comes up now, in one to three plain sentences. Who raised it, on what grounds. No bare IDs, row numbers or file names (ai/gate.md, *Talking to me*).",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "why_it_matters": {
      "description": "What changes in the thesis depending on the answer, in one sentence.",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "question": {
      "description": "The choice itself, ending with a question mark.",
      "type": "string",
      "pattern": "\\?\\s*$"
    },
    "multi_select": {
      "description": "True when the options are independent and several may be chosen.",
      "type": "boolean",
      "default": false
    },
    "options": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 2,
      "maxItems": 4,
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["label", "description", "edits"],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "label": {
            "description": "The action in plain words, one to five words. Never an ID or a code alone.",
            "type": "string",
            "maxLength": 40
          },
          "description": {
            "description": "What choosing it means, and what follows from it for the thesis.",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "recommended": {
            "description": "At most one option per card; listed first.",
            "type": "boolean",
            "default": false
          },
          "why_recommended": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "edits": {
            "description": "The exact edits the option makes. Empty for 'no change'.",
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "oneOf": [
                {
                  "type": "object",
                  "required": ["file", "before", "after"],
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "properties": {
                    "file": {"type": "string"},
                    "before": {"description": "Current text, matching exactly once.", "type": "string"},
                    "after": {"type": "string"}
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "object",
                  "required": ["file", "status"],
                  "additionalProperties": false,
                  "properties": {
                    "file": {"type": "string"},
                    "status": {"enum": ["accepted", "changed", "rejected", "retired"]}
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
